The routine routes are listed with why each falls short:
- the class and subdivision theorems reach classes only;
- norming needs biregularity (Hatami Theorem 2.10(ii));
- the one-side-regular criterion misses the Heawood graph (7 against 35);
- local Sidorenko holds only near the constant graphon;
- the degree-one and bounded-degree reductions stop at Problem 1.5;
- transferring the reported construction gives no leading-order deficit.

The triviality objection (a bare strengthening of Problem 1.5) is answered. Nothing is certified about what routine methods cannot do.

